    /// <summary>
    /// MLEDIT's crosses (CC, OC, MC) and corner joint (CJ) of two multilines against the records AutoCAD 2021 left
    /// (accoreconsole, read back through <c>DxfOut</c> of a <c>Wblock</c>), STANDARD at scale 20 justified at the top. AutoCAD does
    /// not cross the segments the picks lie on but looks at every pair of segments of the two multilines: a pair is crossed
    /// where the lines of both meet on the segment or past the free end of an open multiline (the start of its first, the end
    /// of its last), and of the pairs that can be crossed the one whose meeting is nearest the two picks along the multilines
    /// is taken (the sum of the two distances along them). Where none can, the lines meeting past a vertex of the multiline's
    /// first or last segment while the other multiline runs on past its free end is refused: a cross says <c>Invalid operation
    /// on a self intersecting multiline.</c> and a corner joint says nothing and only puts the first multiline's start caps off;
    /// every other case says <c>These multilines do not intersect.</c>. Each row is the option, the points of the first
    /// multiline, those of the second, where each is picked, and what AutoCAD answered: its message, then the two multilines
    /// each as its flags and its vertices with the stretches of each element after the offset in braces, as
    /// <see cref="MlineJoinNearCornerTests"/> writes them.
    /// </summary>
    public class MlineCrossPairTests
    {
